%I A399301 #14 Sep 14 2026 23:56:43
%S A399301 2,7,19,31,71,103,137,191,233,317,439,577,587,617,709,967,1013,1153,
%T A399301 1319,1321,1499,1543,1663,1789,2003,2029
%N A399301 Primes not in A398545.
%C A399301 a(1) = 2 is trivial, since A398545 concerns odd primes; 2 occurs as a Goldbach prime only for N = 4 = 2 + 2.
%C A399301 Each remaining term lies strictly between two consecutive terms of A398545: if A398545(k-1) < q < A398545(k), then the congruence conditions defining A398545 prohibit q from occurring as an n-th smallest Goldbach prime for every n >= k, while permitting it for smaller n.
%e A399301 a(2) = 7: the primes 3, 5, 7 occupy all residue classes mod 3, so 7 can never be a 3rd (or higher) smallest Goldbach prime, though it does occur as a 2nd smallest, e.g. for 14 = 3 + 11 = 7 + 7.
%Y A399301 Cf. A020481, A398183, A398545.
